{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1526381-new-stv-product-fragile-innocence-a-mechanical-update-for-wod-innocents","id":1526381,"title":"New STV Product: Fragile Innocence, A Mechanical Update for WoD: Innocents","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-12-05T17:24:41-08:00","id":1526381,"title":"New STV Product: Fragile Innocence, A Mechanical Update for WoD: Innocents","content":"<div align=\"center\"><i>This is the story about a kid.</i><br /> <br /> <i>Well, alright, it's the story about a bunch of kids. Stories, really. You know the ones. A kid gets on the bus for school, and never actually gets off. Some teenagers ignore the NO SWIMMING sign at the lake, and no one ever sees them again. A ten-year-old just became the oldest instead of the only, and everyone thinks its her fault when the new baby goes missing. You hear these kinds of stories all the time. They're everywhere. People care about this stuff.</i><br /> <br /> <i>What they don't care about is the truth. Not most of 'em, anyway. At least, they don't believe the truth, and I guess that's all kind of the same thing, isn't it?</i></div> <hr /><br /> Thrown into a strange world with only their friends, a skateboard, and a loyal pet, Innocents are faced with a choice when they encounter the supernatural: do they hide away and try to forget the truth, or do they storm into the haunted house to face whatever horror lies inside?<br /> <br /> <b>Fragile Innocence</b> is a complete guide for playing child protagonists within <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b>, with updates and expansions to the original book in which Innocents were featured, <b>World of Darkness: Innocents</b>. It contains:<ul><li>Updates to systems featured in World of Darkness to make them reflect new rules and systems in Chronicles of Darkness</li> <li>Guides on how to create characters who have less learned skills, different Breaking Points, and different starting stats than traditional characters in <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> games</li> <li>A new system for conflict resolution that appropriately reflects the struggles children often face when trying to establish themselves as someone to be listened to and believed</li> <li>New Merits</li> <li>A guide to creating teenagers, who are caught somewhere between childhood and adulthood, and can be used as supporting or staring characters in various stories</li> </ul><br /> <b>Fragile Innocence </b>is intended to provide updated mechanics for children and teenagers in the Chronicles of Darkness Setting. The topical essays in <b>World of Darkness: Innocents</b> remain useful in second edition and are not duplicated here.<br /> <br /> <br /> <u><b><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/462836/Fragile-Innocence\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#3498DB\">Now available on the Storyteller's Vault.</span></a></b></u>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11893,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11893-tenebra","user":"tenebra","date":". 12-05-2023, 08:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11893-tenebra","name":"tenebra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11893_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-05T17:29:44-08:00","id":1526382,"title":"","content":"congrats tenebra!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key